1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,829
Lesson 4.3: Updating Clinical Data. Part 1: Conditions and Allergies.

2
00:00:08,029 --> 00:00:12,216
After you enroll a scratch patient and complete the initial assessment,

3
00:00:12,256 --> 00:00:17,340
you update their clinical data in ThoroughCare, so it matches PointClickCare.

4
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:25,820
Clinical Data has seven sections. You update five of them, so they match PointClickCare exactly.

5
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:33,767
Conditions and Allergies are in this part. Lab Results, Medications, and Immunizations are in part two.

6
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:40,220
In Conditions, you check three things: the condition, its diagnosis code, and the program.

7
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:46,801
In Allergies, you add only the allergies whose type is Allergy. Intolerances aren't added.

8
00:00:48,801 --> 00:00:52,693
You're in ThoroughCare, on the patient's Care Management tab.

9
00:00:52,943 --> 00:00:59,331
The patient is enrolled in CCM, with their consent, and the initial assessment is done.

10
00:00:59,581 --> 00:01:04,732
Next, you update the patient's clinical data, so it matches PointClickCare.

11
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:11,626
You do all of your work for a patient in two tabs: Care Management, where you are now, and Clinical Data.

12
00:01:11,881 --> 00:01:13,845
Open Clinical Data.

13
00:01:16,768 --> 00:01:25,716
Clinical Data has seven sections: Conditions, Allergies, Lab Results, Medications, Vitals, Immunizations, and Screenings.

14
00:01:25,966 --> 00:01:32,695
You update five of them: Conditions, Allergies, Lab Results, Medications, and Immunizations.

15
00:01:32,945 --> 00:01:37,584
Each one must match the patient's data in PointClickCare exactly.

16
00:01:37,834 --> 00:01:41,811
This part covers the first two: Conditions, and Allergies.

17
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:45,270
Start with Conditions. Click it to open it.

18
00:01:47,834 --> 00:01:53,966
Conditions lists the patient's CCM condition. You added it when you enrolled the patient.

19
00:01:54,216 --> 00:01:55,911
Check three things.

20
00:02:01,274 --> 00:02:05,303
First, the condition: Hypertension (high blood pressure).

21
00:02:05,553 --> 00:02:11,152
Second, the diagnosis code: I10 - Essential (primary) hypertension.

22
00:02:11,402 --> 00:02:16,851
It's the code used for billing, so it must match the code in PointClickCare exactly.

23
00:02:17,117 --> 00:02:19,959
And third, the program: CCM.

24
00:02:23,801 --> 00:02:27,821
If any of these is wrong, remove the condition, and add it again.

25
00:02:28,219 --> 00:02:31,492
To remove it, click the X at the end of the row.

26
00:02:37,298 --> 00:02:39,398
Then click Add condition.

27
00:02:40,701 --> 00:02:43,676
A box opens: Select one to add.

28
00:02:43,926 --> 00:02:48,031
Click it, and type the first letters of the condition: hyper.

29
00:02:49,558 --> 00:02:54,581
Then select Hypertension (High Blood Pressure / HBP / HTN).

30
00:02:54,834 --> 00:03:00,923
The condition is back. Its diagnosis code is empty, and its program says Not Managed.

31
00:03:01,173 --> 00:03:04,766
So find the diagnosis code in PointClickCare.

32
00:03:06,068 --> 00:03:12,520
In PointClickCare, go to the Med Diag tab. It lists the patient's medical diagnoses.

33
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:16,193
Scroll through the list until you find the condition.

34
00:03:16,768 --> 00:03:20,404
Here it is: Essential (primary) hypertension.

35
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:26,578
Its ICD-10 code is I10. That's the exact code you enter in ThoroughCare.

36
00:03:28,682 --> 00:03:32,527
Back in ThoroughCare, click Add From Diagnosis History.

37
00:03:33,668 --> 00:03:36,363
A list of diagnosis codes opens.

38
00:03:36,624 --> 00:03:38,815
Type the code: I10.

39
00:03:39,934 --> 00:03:45,466
I10 - Essential (primary) hypertension is in the patient's Diagnosis History,

40
00:03:45,506 --> 00:03:49,479
and in the codes commonly used for hypertension.

41
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:52,694
If the code you need is in this list, select it.

42
00:03:54,001 --> 00:03:57,912
If it isn't, use the first option in the list: Add New.

43
00:04:00,288 --> 00:04:01,807
Click Add New.

44
00:04:04,934 --> 00:04:10,959
A Diagnosis History window opens, with a box: Search for ICD-10 Code.

45
00:04:11,224 --> 00:04:13,415
Type the code: I10.

46
00:04:14,534 --> 00:04:18,405
Select I10: Essential (primary) hypertension.

47
00:04:18,655 --> 00:04:20,307
Then click Save.

48
00:04:21,434 --> 00:04:24,284
The code now appears next to the condition.

49
00:04:25,601 --> 00:04:28,085
Last, open the Programs list.

50
00:04:28,335 --> 00:04:34,036
The options are CCM, CCO, and BHI. Choose CCM.

51
00:04:36,354 --> 00:04:38,006
Then click Save.

52
00:04:38,256 --> 00:04:40,327
That's all for Conditions.

53
00:04:40,577 --> 00:04:49,013
You add the condition, its code, and the program when you enroll the patient. So usually, you only check them here, and move on.

54
00:04:54,538 --> 00:04:56,979
Next, Allergies. Open it.

55
00:04:59,101 --> 00:05:04,358
If you added the patient's allergies in the initial assessment, they're already listed here.

56
00:05:04,608 --> 00:05:10,399
If not, you add them now. Either way, this list must match PointClickCare exactly.

57
00:05:10,649 --> 00:05:16,695
This one has COVID-19 (Adenovirus) Vaccine. It isn't one of this patient's allergies

58
00:05:16,735 --> 00:05:19,554
in PointClickCare, so remove it.

59
00:05:19,805 --> 00:05:22,428
To delete an allergy, click Remove.

60
00:05:22,974 --> 00:05:25,970
A box asks if you're sure. Click OK.

61
00:05:27,101 --> 00:05:30,539
The allergy is deleted, and the list is empty.

62
00:05:35,082 --> 00:05:38,398
In PointClickCare, open the Allergies tab.

63
00:05:39,534 --> 00:05:42,296
It lists every allergy the patient has.

64
00:05:43,534 --> 00:05:46,871
This patient has two: penicillin, and Lipitor.

65
00:05:47,133 --> 00:05:49,956
Before you add an allergy, check its Type.

66
00:05:50,206 --> 00:05:57,511
Add only the allergies whose type is Allergy. Don't add intolerances, such as lactose intolerance.

67
00:05:57,768 --> 00:06:01,020
Here, both are type Allergy, so you add both.

68
00:06:03,659 --> 00:06:08,575
Start with penicillin. Copy its name, and note its category: Drug.

69
00:06:10,625 --> 00:06:14,858
It was identified on April 21, 2026.

70
00:06:19,990 --> 00:06:22,790
Back in ThoroughCare, click New Allergy.

71
00:06:24,934 --> 00:06:27,944
The Add/Edit Allergy window opens.

72
00:06:28,210 --> 00:06:34,427
Open Category. The options are food, medication, environment, and biologic.

73
00:06:34,677 --> 00:06:39,209
In ThoroughCare, a drug is a medication, so choose medication.

74
00:06:39,475 --> 00:06:44,519
Click Substance, and press Windows key + V to open your clipboard history.

75
00:06:44,772 --> 00:06:47,597
Paste the allergy's name: penicillin.

76
00:06:48,970 --> 00:06:51,198
Then click Date Identified.

77
00:06:56,334 --> 00:07:01,589
Check the date in PointClickCare: April 21, 2026.

78
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:07,070
Back in ThoroughCare, type it: 04/21/2026.

79
00:07:08,415 --> 00:07:13,502
Next, Reaction. In PointClickCare, look at Reaction Manifestation.

80
00:07:15,634 --> 00:07:21,681
If it lists a reaction, such as a skin rash or anaphylaxis, copy it into Reaction.

81
00:07:21,934 --> 00:07:24,973
Here it's empty, so leave Reaction blank.

82
00:07:25,223 --> 00:07:26,982
Then check Active.

83
00:07:29,001 --> 00:07:34,301
Check Critical only when the allergy's severity in PointClickCare is Severe.

84
00:07:35,598 --> 00:07:39,127
Here, it's Unknown, so leave Critical unchecked.

85
00:07:39,377 --> 00:07:41,830
Back in ThoroughCare, click Save.

86
00:07:42,968 --> 00:07:50,913
Penicillin is added: medication, active, not critical, identified 04/21/2026.

87
00:07:51,163 --> 00:07:58,191
Repeat these steps for every allergy in PointClickCare. For this patient, add Lipitor the same way.

88
00:07:58,441 --> 00:08:01,821
When both lists match, move on to Lab Results.

89
00:08:03,234 --> 00:08:04,758
Let's recap.

90
00:08:04,958 --> 00:08:09,234
Open Clinical Data. You update five of its seven sections.

91
00:08:09,434 --> 00:08:14,050
In Conditions, check the condition, the diagnosis code, and the program.

92
00:08:14,090 --> 00:08:18,211
If one is wrong, remove the condition, and add it again.

93
00:08:18,411 --> 00:08:25,520
Find the code in Med Diag in PointClickCare, and add it from Diagnosis History, or with Add New.

94
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:28,518
Set the program to CCM, and save.

95
00:08:28,718 --> 00:08:35,447
In Allergies, make the list match PointClickCare. Add only the allergies whose type is Allergy.

96
00:08:35,647 --> 00:08:41,141
For each one, click New Allergy, and fill in the category, the substance, and the date.

97
00:08:41,181 --> 00:08:46,451
Check Active, and check Critical only if the severity is Severe. Then save.

98
00:08:48,651 --> 00:08:53,780
That's part one. The patient's conditions and allergies match PointClickCare.

99
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:59,067
In part two, you update the other three sections, starting with Lab Results.
